1
00:00:07,739 --> 00:00:11,809
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:12,577 --> 00:00:13,544
So.

3
00:00:13,544 --> 00:00:14,846
Explosives.

4
00:00:16,214 --> 00:00:18,416
Yeah, I think I'm going the wrong way.

5
00:00:19,550 --> 00:00:21,486
I've obviously made a mistake somewhere.

6
00:00:22,020 --> 00:00:26,758
I mean, I haven't seen any dead bodies
lately, or blood smears or bone piles,

7
00:00:26,758 --> 00:00:29,460
and that's usually a
sign the trail's gone cold.

8
00:00:29,460 --> 00:00:31,863
Yeah, see, there's
probably a ladder here.

9
00:00:32,664 --> 00:00:34,365
There's no ladder here.

10
00:00:34,866 --> 00:00:38,302
Just these one-centimeter
rounded grooves to mock me.

11
00:00:38,302 --> 00:00:41,673
See, if I had a grappling hook,
I could just go "whoosh" up there.

12
00:00:41,673 --> 00:00:43,408
Then "whoosh" up there.

13
00:00:43,408 --> 00:00:47,311
Really, you don't need a physics
degree to grasp the concept.

14
00:00:47,311 --> 00:00:51,215
But the fact that I have one
is just insult to injury!

15
00:00:51,215 --> 00:00:55,019
I guess you don't need an architectural
degree to figure things out, either.

16
00:00:55,019 --> 00:00:56,988
I mean, what if this elevator went out?

17
00:00:57,855 --> 00:01:00,792
Or, what if it was planted with explosives?

18
00:01:00,792 --> 00:01:01,826
Can I move this?

19
00:01:03,161 --> 00:01:04,762
That's pretty heavy.

20
00:01:04,762 --> 00:01:07,498
So, the question is,
are these plastic explosives,

21
00:01:07,498 --> 00:01:09,867
which are harmless without a detonator,

22
00:01:09,867 --> 00:01:12,036
or are these maybe
nitroglycerin-based,

23
00:01:12,036 --> 00:01:13,771
where, if I start banging
these crates around,

24
00:01:13,771 --> 00:01:15,506
it's the last thing I do on this Earth?

25
00:01:16,240 --> 00:01:18,176
Well, why take a chance?

26
00:01:18,176 --> 00:01:21,612
If I'm going to level this place,
I'm not going to be half-assed about it.

27
00:01:21,612 --> 00:01:23,247
I'm going to do it right.

28
00:01:23,247 --> 00:01:28,286
I HAVE TO BLOW EVERYTHING UP!
IT'S THE ONLY WAY TO PROVE I'M NOT CRAZY!

29
00:01:28,286 --> 00:01:30,455
Okay, down, down, down, down,
down, down, down, down!

30
00:01:30,455 --> 00:01:34,158
[explosion]
Oh...boy...

31
00:01:34,158 --> 00:01:36,828
I didn't think this through very well.

32
00:01:36,828 --> 00:01:40,932
I can't keep rationalizing away
everything like this or I'm gonna die!

33
00:01:42,734 --> 00:01:45,403
Trinitrotoluene doesn't care
what mood you're in.

34
00:01:47,071 --> 00:01:49,073
What--what's going on?

35
00:01:49,073 --> 00:01:50,541
Why isn't this rubble?

36
00:01:50,541 --> 00:01:54,579
I see stress marks
in the walls, but that's it.

37
00:01:54,579 --> 00:01:57,014
Those weren't firecrackers!

38
00:01:57,014 --> 00:01:58,282
Hey, what's this?

39
00:01:58,282 --> 00:02:01,953
This is...this is a satchel charge!

40
00:02:01,953 --> 00:02:04,756
Oh, that would've been pretty
handy about a minute ago!

41
00:02:04,756 --> 00:02:08,760
Then I could've detonated this
remotely and not risk a cave-in!

42
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:10,695
[rumbling]
...which...may still happen.

43
00:02:10,695 --> 00:02:11,662
[rumbling]
I should go.

44
00:02:11,662 --> 00:02:14,732
Huh, well, looks like
somebody saw a good show.

45
00:02:15,399 --> 00:02:18,836
Okay, going up, yes, up.

46
00:02:18,836 --> 00:02:19,604
UP!

47
00:02:21,239 --> 00:02:23,775
I'm starting to question whether
I ever really did have a life

48
00:02:23,775 --> 00:02:25,343
that wasn't underground.

49
00:02:25,343 --> 00:02:27,612
Things get strange down here.

50
00:02:27,612 --> 00:02:29,347
Ah, electrical arcs.

51
00:02:29,347 --> 00:02:32,583
Being electrocuted is old hat
for me now, alright?

52
00:02:33,417 --> 00:02:35,286
Well, it seems to have a pattern.

53
00:02:36,521 --> 00:02:36,988
Yee!

54
00:02:37,355 --> 00:02:40,057
Don't switch up.
Don't switch up!

55
00:02:41,159 --> 00:02:43,694
Why is it arcing straight into concrete?

56
00:02:43,694 --> 00:02:48,733
So, is my education about electromagnetism
wrong or is the WORLD wrong?

57
00:02:49,267 --> 00:02:49,834
Oh.

58
00:02:50,067 --> 00:02:50,568
Well.

59
00:02:51,135 --> 00:02:51,769
Damn.

60
00:02:52,170 --> 00:02:55,640
I guess I could jump
these, but if I scuff it,

61
00:02:55,640 --> 00:02:58,276
then it's going to hurt
more than a little bit.

62
00:02:58,276 --> 00:03:00,912
I'll play it safe and just crawl under.

63
00:03:00,912 --> 00:03:04,382
Besides, I really can't recall
any safety advice that says

64
00:03:04,382 --> 00:03:06,617
to run and jump around explosives.

65
00:03:06,617 --> 00:03:08,619
That would be dope if they had
something like this

66
00:03:08,619 --> 00:03:10,555
for hurdles at the Olympics, though.

67
00:03:10,555 --> 00:03:13,357
If a runner screwed up,
he would just explode.

68
00:03:13,357 --> 00:03:15,893
I bet the adrenaline would
increase performance.

69
00:03:15,893 --> 00:03:19,630
Huh, I guess the alien disaster
isn't slowing down production any.

70
00:03:19,630 --> 00:03:22,099
Gotta keep those shareholders happy.

71
00:03:22,099 --> 00:03:25,169
Today's episode is brought to
you by the number 8.

72
00:03:25,169 --> 00:03:27,205
Just what are we shipping anyway?

73
00:03:27,205 --> 00:03:28,606
These look like engine parts.

74
00:03:29,307 --> 00:03:30,007
OH GOD!

75
00:03:30,007 --> 00:03:33,010
NO!  STOP!  STOP THAT!  STOP!

76
00:03:33,010 --> 00:03:34,412
What the fuck?!

77
00:03:34,412 --> 00:03:36,647
Did they just pop out of a box?!

78
00:03:36,647 --> 00:03:38,282
Why were they in a box?!

79
00:03:38,282 --> 00:03:40,184
That's Looney Tunes crap!

80
00:03:40,184 --> 00:03:41,385
Jesus!

81
00:03:41,385 --> 00:03:43,955
Well, they caught me off-guard,
I'll give them that.

82
00:03:43,955 --> 00:03:47,391
I wonder if that was their idea or if
it came from up the chain of command.

83
00:03:47,391 --> 00:03:50,494
Yeah, I could envision some
cigar-smoking general ordering this.

84
00:03:51,596 --> 00:03:53,831
"Yah, put two soldiers in a box!

85
00:03:53,831 --> 00:03:56,334
"When the enemy approaches,
they just jump out.

86
00:03:56,334 --> 00:03:57,168
"It's brilliant!"

87
00:03:57,668 --> 00:04:00,037
I bet they're both named Jack, too.

88
00:04:00,037 --> 00:04:01,439
Hey, what's this do?

89
00:04:01,439 --> 00:04:03,975
Oh.  Great.  That helps a lot.

90
00:04:03,975 --> 00:04:06,510
Maybe I should've taken the
tram, I don't know.

91
00:04:06,510 --> 00:04:09,981
Then I could've loaded it up with dead
bodies, and just sent it forward.

92
00:04:09,981 --> 00:04:12,416
That would probably creep out
everybody down the line.

93
00:04:12,416 --> 00:04:13,851
That would creep me out.

94
00:04:13,851 --> 00:04:17,788
If I was working in the lab and this
cartful of dead scientists just rolled in.

95
00:04:17,788 --> 00:04:20,057
It's a real conversation-stopper.

96
00:04:20,057 --> 00:04:22,793
Yeah, these goons write
"Yore dead, Freeman" on the wall,

97
00:04:22,793 --> 00:04:24,962
so I send them back a cartful of bodies.

98
00:04:24,962 --> 00:04:26,230
Who wins then?

99
00:04:26,230 --> 00:04:30,368
Psychological warfare worked for
Vlad the Impaler, it can work for me, too.

100
00:04:30,368 --> 00:04:34,906
Okay, looks like more
crates and lasers that way,

101
00:04:34,906 --> 00:04:36,674
let's see what's over this way.

102
00:04:37,909 --> 00:04:40,011
Yeah, I'm not going this way.

103
00:04:40,011 --> 00:04:42,380
All right, so this must be the right way.

104
00:04:42,380 --> 00:04:43,848
That was easy to figure out.

105
00:04:44,382 --> 00:04:45,182
So, I guess that--

106
00:04:45,716 --> 00:04:47,385
Stupid flashlight.

107
00:04:47,385 --> 00:04:51,923
Huh, I guess I'm pretty lucky the
power's still working down here.

108
00:04:51,923 --> 00:04:54,558
Because, if it went out and the
flashlight stopped working,

109
00:04:54,558 --> 00:04:58,562
I guess I'd have to navigate my
way by the light of my muzzle flashes,

110
00:04:58,562 --> 00:05:02,199
which would be less-than-ideal
for a lot of reasons.

111
00:05:02,199 --> 00:05:05,736
"Sector E Material Transfer B"
Yeah, I'm lost.

112
00:05:05,736 --> 00:05:07,939
This doesn't mean anything.

113
00:05:07,939 --> 00:05:10,107
Oh, what the hell, a dead end?

114
00:05:10,107 --> 00:05:12,009
But, it's Sector E!

115
00:05:12,009 --> 00:05:13,778
It goes down again?

116
00:05:13,778 --> 00:05:15,913
How is that even possible?

117
00:05:15,913 --> 00:05:19,050
Well, I don't want to turn around.
That's even more depressing.

118
00:05:19,750 --> 00:05:22,586
Yep.  Going down.

119
00:05:22,586 --> 00:05:24,588
God dammit, I want some pills.

120
00:05:25,589 --> 00:05:26,624
All right...

121
00:05:27,291 --> 00:05:30,027
I guess I could just pretend I'm
some giant submarine,

122
00:05:30,027 --> 00:05:32,430
but that wouldn't make
me feel any better.

123
00:05:32,430 --> 00:05:35,132
Whoa! Lots of lasers.

124
00:05:35,132 --> 00:05:36,467
Watch your step.

125
00:05:37,134 --> 00:05:39,337
So, I guess let's check out the--

126
00:05:39,337 --> 00:05:42,139
WHOA-HO-HO-HO-HO, what is that?

127
00:05:42,139 --> 00:05:44,742
Hell's coat rack, I don't think so!

128
00:05:45,309 --> 00:05:46,043
Yeah!

129
00:05:46,043 --> 00:05:46,777
AAAH!

130
00:05:46,777 --> 00:05:49,580
DIE DIE DIE DIE DIE DIE DIE!

131
00:05:50,982 --> 00:05:53,517
Okay.  I think I got them.

132
00:05:53,517 --> 00:05:54,785
They flanked me.

133
00:05:54,785 --> 00:05:56,787
Which is why I know there's
one under HERE!

134
00:05:57,555 --> 00:05:58,990
Oh.  Maybe not.

135
00:05:58,990 --> 00:06:00,992
I don't think they can fit in
the drawer.

136
00:06:00,992 --> 00:06:02,793
Even the extra long one.

137
00:06:02,793 --> 00:06:06,263
"Well, here we are in New Mexico,
back on the Laser Corral,

138
00:06:06,263 --> 00:06:10,568
"roundin' up aliens so we can, well,
I dunno what we're gonna do with them."

139
00:06:10,568 --> 00:06:13,070
Okay, I don't want to try and do
a roll through here.

140
00:06:13,070 --> 00:06:14,872
There's no room for error if I'm off.

141
00:06:16,707 --> 00:06:18,275
"Space varmints!"

142
00:06:18,275 --> 00:06:19,744
Oh, hey, grenades.

143
00:06:19,744 --> 00:06:21,846
Glad I didn't hit them with my shotgun.

144
00:06:21,846 --> 00:06:25,383
Okay, I'm going to pretend there's a world
where not all glass is bulletproof.

145
00:06:26,283 --> 00:06:28,085
Hey!  Look at that!

146
00:06:28,085 --> 00:06:30,054
That's the power of imagination.

147
00:06:30,821 --> 00:06:32,823
Hah!  I bypassed it.

148
00:06:32,823 --> 00:06:34,258
No one can cage me.

149
00:06:34,592 --> 00:06:35,993
Kind of sad, though.

150
00:06:35,993 --> 00:06:39,096
Here we have this giant underground
complex and all these lasers,

151
00:06:39,096 --> 00:06:41,766
and instead of having a rave,
we're using it for evil.

152
00:06:41,766 --> 00:06:43,234
Oop, speak of the devil.

153
00:06:45,036 --> 00:06:47,271
Yeah, I'm pretty sure he saw me.

154
00:06:48,039 --> 00:06:49,040
Or did he?

155
00:06:51,375 --> 00:06:53,144
Yeah, I think he saw me.

156
00:06:54,145 --> 00:06:57,048
I wonder if they're like infants
and think, when they can't see me,

157
00:06:57,048 --> 00:06:58,783
that I've literally disappeared.

158
00:07:00,518 --> 00:07:02,453
No, I guess they're more
developed than that.

159
00:07:04,321 --> 00:07:08,325
God, one of them's in a bunker;
this is going to take all day.

160
00:07:08,325 --> 00:07:09,326
I'm not touching you!

161
00:07:09,693 --> 00:07:10,528
I'm not touching you!

162
00:07:10,961 --> 00:07:13,697
I guess that game doesn't really
work from ten yards away.

163
00:07:14,799 --> 00:07:17,701
Man, killing the soldiers is one
of those chores where,

164
00:07:17,701 --> 00:07:20,871
if I had any option at all,
I'd just put it off.

165
00:07:20,871 --> 00:07:22,540
Hope it solves--Oh shit!

166
00:07:22,540 --> 00:07:23,874
Back, back, back!

167
00:07:23,874 --> 00:07:27,178
Actually, now would be a GREAT
time for the lights to go out.

168
00:07:27,178 --> 00:07:29,413
I could make ghost noises and he
might stop firing.

169
00:07:30,181 --> 00:07:31,549
You can't kill a ghost!

170
00:07:31,916 --> 00:07:33,250
Okay, this isn't working.

171
00:07:33,250 --> 00:07:35,252
I'm going to have to get closer.

172
00:07:35,252 --> 00:07:37,521
[straining]

173
00:07:37,521 --> 00:07:38,989
[exhaling]

174
00:07:38,989 --> 00:07:42,126
Out of the frying pan, into
another frying pan.

175
00:07:42,993 --> 00:07:45,663
God, I'm really slogging through here,

176
00:07:45,663 --> 00:07:47,198
going inch by inch,

177
00:07:47,198 --> 00:07:49,467
laying down a lot of gunfire...

178
00:07:49,467 --> 00:07:52,303
So that probably means that
this is really just a dead end,

179
00:07:52,303 --> 00:07:54,538
and I've been taking the wrong
path this whole time

180
00:07:54,538 --> 00:07:56,006
since that fork in the track.

181
00:07:56,006 --> 00:07:57,208
I'm going to kill all these people

182
00:07:57,208 --> 00:08:00,111
only to find out they were
guarding some janitor's closet.

183
00:08:00,111 --> 00:08:01,579
Dammit, I can't see anything.

184
00:08:03,280 --> 00:08:04,081
Oh.

185
00:08:04,081 --> 00:08:04,849
That's right.

186
00:08:05,483 --> 00:08:06,617
Stay down.

187
00:08:07,218 --> 00:08:09,954
Well, I probably creeped him out
by getting so close to him.

188
00:08:09,954 --> 00:08:12,923
This is sort of like playing "Marco Polo",
except we don't say anything,

189
00:08:12,923 --> 00:08:14,458
we just shoot at each other.

190
00:08:14,458 --> 00:08:15,759
And it's more intense.

191
00:08:15,759 --> 00:08:16,594
Marco!

192
00:08:16,927 --> 00:08:19,230
Oh, wait, he's the blind one.
So that means I'm "Polo".

193
00:08:19,230 --> 00:08:19,797
Shit.

194
00:08:20,131 --> 00:08:20,798
Polo!

195
00:08:23,767 --> 00:08:24,401
Polo!

196
00:08:24,969 --> 00:08:25,402
[crackling noise]
What?

197
00:08:25,402 --> 00:08:25,870
[crackling noise]

198
00:08:25,870 --> 00:08:27,138
[crackling noise]
Oh, cool!  I won!

199
00:08:27,138 --> 00:08:28,839
[crackling noise]
Time for the victory dance!

200
00:08:28,839 --> 00:08:31,142
[crackling noise]
Dahdah, dah dah...wait, wait.

201
00:08:31,142 --> 00:08:32,877
[crackling noise]
There could still be some more players.

202
00:08:32,877 --> 00:08:35,246
[crackling noise]
And what the hell is that crackling sound?

203
00:08:35,246 --> 00:08:36,614
[crackling noise]
Yah!

204
00:08:36,614 --> 00:08:38,415
[crackling noise]
So, you're the behind all this!

205
00:08:41,152 --> 00:08:42,386
Not anymore.

206
00:08:43,420 --> 00:08:47,825
Okay, let's see if I can go another ten
yards without running into any soldiers.

207
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:51,795
HECU #1: So, who is this guy, Freeman?
Nope.

208
00:08:51,795 --> 00:08:54,798
HECU #2: They say he was at Ground Zero.
Hey, I'm outside!

209
00:08:54,798 --> 00:08:59,503
HECU #1: Science Team?  You think he
was responsible? Sabotage, maybe?

210
00:08:59,503 --> 00:09:01,605
HECU #2: Yeah, maybe.
No!  NO!

211
00:09:01,605 --> 00:09:03,807
HECU #2: All I know for sure is
he's been killing my buddies.

212
00:09:03,807 --> 00:09:06,544
HECU #1: Oh yeah, he'll pay.
Oh...ri-

213
00:09:06,544 --> 00:09:08,078
HECU #1: He will definitely p--

214
00:09:10,080 --> 00:09:12,650
There!  That's for trying to guilt trip me!

215
00:09:12,650 --> 00:09:14,985
Yeah, the Big Bad Freeman!

216
00:09:14,985 --> 00:09:18,522
OF COURSE! YOU GUYS DIDN'T START SHIT!

217
00:09:18,522 --> 00:09:21,392
I don't know why I'm a patsy,
but I'm not going to take it.

218
00:09:21,392 --> 00:09:22,893
Fuck the system!

219
00:09:22,893 --> 00:09:26,363
Ahh, I'm outside. All right!

220
00:09:26,363 --> 00:09:29,833
Okay, blast door, blast door. This way.

221
00:09:29,833 --> 00:09:32,102
Man, I can't believe it's night already.

222
00:09:32,102 --> 00:09:34,405
Wait, are these all closed down?

223
00:09:34,405 --> 00:09:36,407
Fine, I'll climb out, I don't care.

224
00:09:37,374 --> 00:09:38,742
Here we go.

225
00:09:38,742 --> 00:09:45,015
[straining]

226
00:09:45,015 --> 00:09:47,952
Christ! The sandstone just breaks off.

227
00:09:47,952 --> 00:09:49,253
I'll find another way.

228
00:09:50,321 --> 00:09:51,689
I need a rope.

229
00:09:51,689 --> 00:09:55,859
Maybe I can strip down the soldiers'
uniforms and splice one together
out of it.

230
00:09:55,859 --> 00:09:57,861
But that's going to take a while.

231
00:09:57,861 --> 00:09:59,029
Nice night out, though.

232
00:09:59,863 --> 00:10:01,098
Is that a full moon?

233
00:10:01,932 --> 00:10:06,403
Awoooooooooooooooooo!

234
00:10:08,205 --> 00:10:12,710
That security guy said this track would
take me straight to the surface.

235
00:10:12,710 --> 00:10:13,777
Okay.

236
00:10:13,777 --> 00:10:16,801
Now what was the LONG way to the surface?

